==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Miyamoto''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Miyamoto''' at level 30 using XP, [[Catfruit]] and [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Musashi Miyamoto is a rather situational backliner, primarily due to his niche being covered by many other units that are much more accessible and tend to do the job just as well, if not better, though in the right scenarios he can absolutely tear through his targets with ease.

Though his abilities do form a good matchup against Dark enemies, able to tank them briefly and do extreme damage, these are unfortunately limited by his Single Attack (even if his fast attack rate is factored in). Many Dark enemies are short-ranged, are spammed in huge hordes, and have enough DPS to cut through him as easily as other units if they are not eliminated quickly. As a result, he is very often outperformed by [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], whose short-ranged Area Attacks can easily destroy many at once.

His generalist value is also lacking, as outside of his niche he's easily replaceable by general backliners like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]], as his single target greatly limits his seemingly high DPS. He does, however, have a point in his favor when up against Darks that tend to appear as bulky singular threats or those with high range, particularly [[Dark Otter]], [[Le'noir]], [[Razorback]], [[Bun Bun Black]],  [[Ragin' Gory]] and especially [[Masked Okame]].

His weakness of Single Attack is less apparent later on into the game, similar to [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]], as the aforementioned Dark enemies will often appear with less support, allowing Miyamoto to get hits in much more easily, especially in Crowned [[Uncanny Legends]] where enemies such as Dark Otter and Bun Bun Black have overly bloated health to where even Pizza Cat may struggle alone.

===True Form===
Immortal Miyamoto's main buffs are an increase to already high attack and HP, allowing for even greater tanking and damage to the bulkier Dark enemies in the game. This may improve the aforementioned advantages against Le'noir and Razorback, though he already did quite well against them.

He gains immunity to Slow and Weaken, both of which are niche but quite useful. The former is useful in [[Croakley]] stages, though he is generally a niche pick in those stages. The latter, however, helps against [[Dark Dober]], whose range and resistances can make it troublesome. Dark Dober is rarely supported by peon spam and is thus one of Immortal Miyamoto's better matchups. While more niche, [[Crocodylidae Kurocroc]] is also made easier.

Finally, as with [[High Lord Babel (Legend Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Babel]], Immortal Miyamoto gets Colossus Slayer. With him being only an average generalist at best, his optimal target is [[Le'Grim]], the only Dark/Colossus enemy in this game, which he performs well against even before True Form, as Le'Grim comes with few supporting peons. Slow Immunity further improves his matchup, allowing him to melt through Le'Grim with terrifying ease.

