==Trivia==
*[[wikipedia:Miyamoto Musashi|Miyamoto Musashi]] (also known as Shinmen Takezō, Miyamoto Bennosukea) was a Japanese dual swordsman, philosopher, writer, and rōnin. Although family names come first in Japanese, the unit's name wasn't changed to Miyamoto Musashi in English, possibly to reduce confusion with [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Miyamoku Musashi]].
**The "Gonekosho" (五猫書) in Immortal Miyamoto's Japanese description is a reference to ''[[wikipedia:The Book of Five Rings|The Book of Five Rings]]'' (五輪書 ''Go Rin no Sho''), a strategy and martial arts book Musashi wrote at the end of his life. The joke is that 猫 ''neko'' means cat.
*Nichirin means "sun", Getsurin means "full moon" or "round moon".
*Although Musashi Miyamoto "travelled to the realm of carnage", this most likely has no relation to the [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]] [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]], which isn't mentioned in his Japanese description and has a different name in [[BCJP]] (修羅の道 ''Shuro no Michi'', "Path of Carnage").
*Musashi Miyamoto and [[Jeanne (Legend Rare Cat)|Jeanne]] were the first units to have the [[Insane Damage]] ability.
*Unlike his Normal and Evolved forms, Immortal Miyamoto is not scaled down to be more visible on screen when his description is hidden in the Cat Guide.

